    <string name="error_suggestions_heading">Suggestions</string>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_underage">
        <item>Your Apple ID may be below the required age to use developer services.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_account_locked">
        <item>Don\'t panic! This usually occurs after multiple failed login attempts, but it is completely harmless.</item>
        <item>Visit ((link:https://iforgot.apple.com/)) to unlock your account.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_auth">
        <item>Make sure your credentials are correct and try again, even if they were correct.</item>
        <item>If the issue persists, try using another Apple ID.</item>
        <item>Security Key 2FA is not supported. If possible, use an Apple ID with no 2FA or with trusted device 2FA.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_download">
        <item>Download SideStore manually from ((link:https://github.com/SideStore/SideStore/releases)) and use the \"Import IPA\" button to install it.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_house_arrest">
        <item>[ios::26.3]Ensure your device is not on a developer beta of iOS 26.3, as it has a bug with house arrest</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_pairing">
        <item>Try reconnecting the device and running the action again.</item>
        <item>Ensure your device has a passcode set.</item>
        <item>Ensure your device is connected via USB, not wirelessly.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_canceled">
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_operation_update">
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_usbmuxd">
        <item>[platform::windows]Ensure you have ((link:https://apple.co/ms:iTunes)) installed and check that it can detect your device.</item>
        <item>[platform::windows]Uninstall iTunes and Apple Mobile Device Support, then install \"Apple Devices\" from the Microsoft Store.</item>
        <item>[platform::linux]Make sure usbmuxd is installed and running.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_trust">
        <item>Unlock your device, go to the home screen, and accept any trust prompts that appear.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_device_coms">
        <item>Ensure your device is properly connected to your computer.</item>
        <item>Unplug and reconnect the device. If the issue persists, try a different USB port and cable.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_not_logged_in">
        <item>Sign in to your Apple ID first.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_no_device_selected">
        <item>Select a device before continuing.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_anisette">
        <item>Ensure your computer is connected to the internet.</item>
        <item>Change your anisette server. Try several different servers.</item>
        <item>Make sure you can access ((link:%1$s)) in a browser.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_keyring">
        <item>Try enabling \"Don\'t use keyring\" in settings to bypass this issue. Note that this is less secure.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_misc">
        <item>Try again. Restarting the app, your computer, and/or your phone may also help.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_admin">
        <item>Try running the app with elevated permissions (as administrator/root).</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_filesystem">
        <item>Make sure iloader has permission to read and write files on your system.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_not_enough_app_ids">
        <item>You do not have enough App IDs available to install this app.</item>
        <item>Wait for App IDs to expire after 7 days (cannot be deleted sooner), then try again.</item>
        <item>Installing apps from SideStore sometimes allows you to use less App IDs, so try installing from there instead.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="error_suggestions_max_apps">
        <item>You can only have 3 sideloaded apps installed at a time with a free Apple ID.</item>
        <item>Delete other sideloaded apps to free up space for this one.</item>
        <item>Expired apps still count towards the 3 app limit.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string name="error_support_message">If the issue persists, press \"Copy to clipboard\" and send the copied error to the &lt;discord&gt;Discord&lt;/discord&gt; or a &lt;github&gt;GitHub issue&lt;/github&gt; for support.</string>
